Knowledge Retrieval

Product Guidance

Recommendation Logic

Booking Flow

Confirmation

Human Escalation

4.2 Conversational Product Flow

User → Query
↓
Intent Classification
↓
If informational → RAG Retrieval → Response
If comparison → Structured RAG → Response
If buying intent → Recommendation Node
If booking intent → Booking Workflow

4.3 Appointment Booking Workflow (Deterministic)

State 1: Detect Booking Intent
State 2: Extract Date/Time Preferences
State 3: Call Availability Tool
State 4: Offer Available Slots
State 5: Confirm Slot
State 6: Create Calendar Event
State 7: Generate Google Meet Link
State 8: Return Confirmation

Safety Features:

Strict tool schemas

Server-side parameter validation

Retry logic

Timezone normalization

Tenant-specific calendar mapping

4.4 Tooling Layer

Tools exposed to the agent:

Check Availability

Create Event

Reschedule Event

Cancel Event

Retrieve Product Data

Escalate to Human

Each tool:

Validates inputs server-side

Logs usage

Enforces tenant isolation

5. Google Calendar & Meet Integration

Authentication Strategy:

OAuth per tenant user (recommended for SaaS)

Secure refresh token storage

Scoped access for Calendar events

When booking:

Create event via Calendar API

Include conference data

Automatically attach Google Meet link

Store event metadata in Vectriva DB

